<article class="env-lemma" id="08NI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08NI">Lemma <span data-tag="08NI">15.5.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $I$ be a finite set. Suppose given a cartesian diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \prod B_ i &  \prod A_ i \ar[l]^{\prod \varphi _ i} \\  Q \ar[u]^{\prod \psi _ i} &  P \ar[u] \ar[l] }  \]
</div>
  <p> with $\psi _ i$ and $\varphi _ i$ surjective, and $Q$, $A_ i$, $B_ i$ of finite type over $R$. Then $P$ is of finite type over $R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00IT" data-tag="00IT">15.5.1</a> and induction on the size of $I$. Namely, let $I = I' \amalg \{ i_0\} $. Let $P'$ be the ring defined by the diagram of the lemma using $I'$. Then $P'$ is of finite type by induction hypothesis. Finally, $P$ sits in a fibre product diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ B_{i_0} &  A_{i_0} \ar[l] \\  P' \ar[u] &  P \ar[u] \ar[l] &  }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       to which the lemma applies. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>